Subject: Rotate the counted loop's test to the latch

What this does
  Rotate the counted loop's test to the latch.

Why we need it
  The loop is test-at-top with an unconditional back edge to the test, so each iteration runs the test (not taken) and the jump (taken).

What it adds
  An IR pass duplicates the test at the latch with the inverted sense, branching back to the body, when the back edge's target is exactly one compare-and-branch, only the entry and the latch reach it, and the exit immediately follows; the `_s` compare family also gets the Step 2 int-only fast path. The original test stays and runs once on entry.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
